# DriftGuard workspace-level .gitignore
# Keep source, specifications, steering, lock files, fixtures, and documentation tracked.

# === Operating systems and editors ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# === Python caches and local environments ===
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/

# === Terraform working data and local state ===
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfplan
**/crash.log
**/crash.*.log
**/plans/
# Do NOT ignore .terraform.lock.hcl - provider selections must be reviewed and committed.

# === Local secrets and environment files ===
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret
*.pem
*.key

# === Tool output and generated artifacts ===
**/coverage.xml
**/test-results/
**/reports/
*.log
**/*-out.txt
**/*-err.txt

# === Workspace-local scratch files (not project deliverables) ===
note.txt
todo.md
REVIEW_FINDINGS.md
SWE_DevOps_AWS_Portfolio_Roadmap.md

# === Kiro internal specs (planning documents, not shipped code) ===
.kiro/specs/gitops-platform/tasks.md

# === Personal/portfolio content (not part of the platform) ===
posts/

# === Architecture diagram generators (dev-only tooling, not runtime) ===
docs/architecture/generate_architecture.py
docs/architecture/embed_icons_in_svg.py
docs/architecture/diagrams/
